    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd">
<en-note><blockquote>my note: incubator house covers Aug-Nov. this is for after, if we stay. Inner Sunset / Cole Valley look right (park for running, N-Judah).</blockquote><hr/><h3>SF neighborhoods for first-time renters</h3><div>Bay Rent Guide, July 2026</div><div><br/></div><div><b>Inner Sunset.</b> Fog, Golden Gate Park on the doorstep, the N-Judah to downtown. Studios and one-bedrooms are a bit cheaper than the eastern neighborhoods. Good for people who run or have a dog.</div><div><br/></div><div><b>Cole Valley.</b> Small, quiet, walkable, close to the park and the N line. Fewer listings, they go fast.</div><div><br/></div><div><b>Mission / Mission Dolores.</b> Sunniest weather in the city, lots of food, more noise. Close to BART for the East Bay and the airport.</div><div><br/></div><div><b>SoMa / Mission Bay.</b> Newer buildings with amenities and higher rents. Close to Caltrain and many offices; quieter at night than you'd expect.</div><div><br/></div><div><b>Richmond.</b> Longer commute downtown, more space for the money, near the park and the ocean.</div><div><br/></div><div>Tips: listings that ask for deposits before a viewing are scams. Expect to show income or a guarantor. Ask whether the unit is rent-controlled (generally buildings first occupied before mid-1979).</div></en-note>]]>
    </content>
  </note>
</en-export>
